presence":[{"entity_id":"customary","role":"present"}]},{"controller_id":"cod-pnc","sovereign_id":"cod","status":"dominant","confidence":"medium","basis":"default_state_presence","as_of":"2026-10-01","zone":"Monkoto town (territory seat, GRID3 locality 'Iccn' at the Salonga National Park station)","evidence":"Territory administrative seat with PNC territorial command and courts; the ICCN/Salonga National Park station (armed eco-guards) is located here but its rangers operate mainly inside the park. No armed group is known to operate in Monkoto territory. No web sources could be retrieved in this run (search budget exhausted; park and news sites blocked), so the assessment rests on the absence of known armed-group activity in Monkoto territory and Tshuapa province.","unit":"CD4507-monkoto","run_id":"drc-swarm-1","presence":[{"entity_id":"cod-iccn","role":"present"}]}],"sources":{},"units":{"CD4507-monkoto":"Monkoto territory (Tshuapa) lies in the central Congo basin around Salonga National Park, far from the eastern conflict zones, and no armed group is known to hold territory there. Monkoto town, the territory seat, is administered by the state with the PNC as the main day-to-day force; the ICCN park station and its armed eco-guards are also based there. Rural villages have very thin state presence and rely on customary authorities, with eco-guard patrols around the park; poaching occurs but no non-state actor exercises control. Web research was unavailable for this run, so confidence is medium for Monkoto town and low elsewhere."}}